From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: the guest's pointer as the Mac's cursor (experimental)

What: with OMACVM_HW_CURSOR=1 (OmacVM.app: the hidden macPointer
setting, off by default) the image the guest puts on virtio-gpu's cursor plane
becomes the Mac's own cursor over the VM's windows (an NSCursor in the
image's size in points, hot spot from the guest). The Mac's cursor is not
hidden then; an empty cursor stands in while the guest hides its pointer
on every output; the arrow comes back when the VM lets go of the pointer.
The extra outputs' windows (one per display) report their cursor plane
too. QEMU's own pointer layer (the image drawn where the guest says) stays
off while the Mac's cursor carries it. Rules: ui/omacvm-hw-cursor.h.

Why: Omarchy draws its pointer into the picture (software cursor), so a
move waits for a whole guest frame and its present, and where the VM's
window meets the notch strip, Omanotch or another display one pointer
hides while the other is still a frame behind (the pointer flickers).
The guest asks for its hardware cursor only with the app's setting
(SMBIOS omacvm.hwcursor=1 -> /run/omacvm/host.env -> omacvm_app.lua).

Until the guest's first image after a reset, and with a relative pointer
(games), nothing changes: the hello of Omarchy's display agent and
show-cursor decide as before. The full-screen pointer guard sees a shown
Mac cursor and follows the guest's pointer (as with show-cursor=on).
Image updates are coalesced: only the newest queued one makes a cursor.
Known limits: a guest that warps its pointer (Hyprland's warps are off in
Omarchy) is back under the Mac's cursor at the next motion. Hyprland 0.56.2
in Omarchy does not use the cursor plane on virtio-gpu yet (no cursor
command reaches QEMU: Linux hides a virtual GPU's cursor plane from atomic
clients without DRM_CLIENT_CAP_CURSOR_PLANE_HOTSPOT, which aquamarine does
not set), so with it this changes nothing today.

Upstream: not sent (OmacVM's pointer policy; upstream draws the image in
a layer at the guest's place).
Test: Tests/display/test-hw-cursor.sh (the rules, build time and CI);
src/tests/input-latency-vm.sh --hw-cursor (a VM: the image arrives, the
Mac's cursor carries it, pointer latency). Applies after
omacvm-cocoa-boot-splash.patch.

